%[text] %[text:anchor:T_C189B5B8] # Interpolation Using Splines
%[text] [⇦ Main Menu](file:../../MainMenu.m)
%[text] Interpolation to determine unknown values between known points is a standard tool for engineers and scientists. Interpolation by splines is one common method of determining a continuous function through discrete data. There are many different algorithms for determining a spline that allow you to preserve various properties such as smoothness or curvature. All splines pass directly through the known datapoints. 
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![A rough outline of a hand](text:image:8447)
%[text] Interpolation between known values can provide a practical, scalable, and controllable way to describe a continuous function while preserving chosen properties. 
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] This live script is intended to be used with the code visible and output inline. On the **View** tab of the MATLAB Toolstrip, in the **View** section, select **Output Inline**. Alternately, select **Output Inline** using the icon ![live script output inline icon](text:image:3cea) at the top right of the Live Editor pane.
